{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (in the 2000s).\n\nLet me verify the key connection: In 2019 (when \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" was published), the Man Booker International Prize was won by a book released the preceding year (2018). That winner was \"Celestial Bodies\" by Jokha Alharthi, translated by Marilyn Booth. Let me verify this and check the city connection.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize 2019 winner Celestial Bodies Jokha Alharthi\", \"Jokha Alharthi born city Oman biography\", \"Celestial Bodies published 2018 2019 Jokha Alharthi\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_3f4cb11efac84b85884e4365","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma grew up city Akure biography childhood\", \"Chigozie Obioma early life Nigeria hometown\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_fe039acb848a455cb5801dbd","index":1,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789472820,"id":"chatcmpl-53fc3afd-12b0-9688-b64e-03b79f09f8bb","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":20960,"completion_tokens":258,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":21218,"cached_tokens":14848,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":14848},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}